there are 2.7 million job postings  requiring project management skills and  more than 70 of them are non-project  manager roles  whether it is a product manager a  developer or a manager of those roles it  is apparent that they often if not  always have to wear a project manager  hat  to succeed projects require an ongoing  battle against a host of challenges such  as changing priorities tightening  deadlines limited resources and  conflicting interests of key  stakeholders  it begs the question how can you  successfully manage projects or lead a  high performance team in today's dynamic  digital world that's why udacity has  created the digital project management  nanodegree program  this nanodegree offers hands-on learning  with real-life digital projects and  digital toolkits to identify compelling  digital methodologies and tools to drive  success  learners will be able to define project  scopes precisely to build resource plans  toward successful outcomes apply best  practices and problem solving strategies  to manage key stakeholders leverage  metrics and emotional intelligence to  ensure the quality of project outcomes  and maximize team performance  are you ready to build impactful digital  project management skills to advance  your career and lead a high performance  team in the digital age  enroll today in our nanodegree to  advance your career in project  management
 

